    {
      "id": 66927,
      "name": "Pydro",
      "username": "Pydro",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-07-19T17:19:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I agree. It is just like movies, you have to find a reviewer who has the same tastes as you. With me, it goes a step further. There are a lot of games I like that are rated highly, but they just don't get to the table. To me, what gets to the table and how often is much more important than actual ratings (either mine or BGGs). However, what gets to the table is often based on the group, not the ratings. I would rather buy a game that I \"just\" like and always play, than a game that I \"love\", but gathers dust on the shelf.</p><p>i do think it is a good judge of how popular the game is, and that is great for GtG.</p><p>Since we are talking about games that not everyone likes, here is a Dice Tower episode: Top 10 overrated games:</p><p><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h-8k9Auuw5g\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h-8k9Auuw5g</a></p><p>EDIT: I might get shot for saying this, but SotM is not my favorite game. Still rated highly, but not my absolutely favorite game.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:44:46.547Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
